Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:34:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] nouveau: keep H.264 references in the same VP slot

VP3 to VP5 identify reference pictures by their slot (fifo_idx), and the
motion vectors stored with each picture refer to those slots. ffmpeg
puts the newest reference first, so the slots shift and B frames with
temporal direct prediction use the wrong pictures, which shows as blocks
in moving areas.

Keep each reference in the slot it already had and put new references
in free slots.

Cc: mesa-stable
Tested-by: Youssef Mahmoud <youssefma255681@gmail.com>
Tested-by: MrNoname3 <1271030-MrNonam3@users.noreply.gitlab.freedesktop.org>
