Subject: [PATCH 5/8] nouveau: pick the vc1 microcode for each picture type

nouveau loads vuc-vc1-0 for every VC-1 picture. NVIDIA's driver loads
vuc-vc1-1 for fields and vuc-vc1-2 for interlaced frames: with the
progressive one, VP decodes the second field of a frame wrongly, and the
frames after it too, and a stream mixing fields with interlaced frames
hangs it.

Load all three and pick one for each picture. Where this is untested
(VP3 and VP5) or vuc-vc1-1 or 2 is missing, refuse interlaced pictures
instead, so that end_frame fails and the application can fall back to
software decoding.

