Subject: [PATCH 7/8] nouveau: don't advertise H.264 High 10, 4:2:2 and 4:4:4

The VP2 to VP5 decoders only handle 8-bit 4:2:0 H.264: they take NV12
surfaces only and never read the bit depth or chroma format. Both
get_video_param functions still report every H.264 profile as supported,
so the VA frontend lists VAProfileH264High10 and FFmpeg uses it for
10-bit streams instead of decoding them in software.

Only report H.264 profiles up to High.

